WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.120
hello and welcome to my latest leaders briefing&nbsp;
i'm currently at our offices here at mill lane&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.880
in Wingerworth where at the moment we're flying&nbsp;
the Ukrainian flag in solidarity with the people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.440
of Ukraine and i think i speak on behalf&nbsp;
of all of us when i say how shocked and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:22.960
saddened we are by the ongoing situation over in&nbsp;
Ukraine and how i'm sure all of us will want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.920
to make it known that we stand with the&nbsp;
people of Ukraine we certainly have at our&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:33.520
recent full council meeting and also as a&nbsp;
council we're looking very closely at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.760
government's homes for Ukraine scheme at the&nbsp;
moment to see how we can support refugees that are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.880
clearly fleeing such a horrible&nbsp;
horrible situation over there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.800
we i also want to say a huge huge thank you to all&nbsp;
the residents and community groups and businesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:55.360
who have been doing so much to support the people&nbsp;
of Ukraine with generous donations of items and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.760
money and all of those sorts of things so i&nbsp;
just want to say a huge thank you for that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:04.480
and we've been getting some our inquiries&nbsp;
ourselves as a council about how people can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:08.880
help and we're certainly encouraging people&nbsp;
to go on the disasters emergency committee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:15.440
website and donate via that means that seems to be&nbsp;
the message that we're getting that donations via&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:20.800
the disasters emergency committee is the best way&nbsp;
that you can get help to the people of Ukraine so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:26.080
please do continue to do all the amazing things&nbsp;
that you're doing and continue to give generously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:31.120
to help in this humanitarian crisis moving on to&nbsp;
a bit of different news i'm sure many of you will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:37.440
have received your Council tax bills through the&nbsp;
post recently it is the budget setting season for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:43.600
many councils across the country and we've taken&nbsp;
the the difficult decision to increase council tax&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:50.640
by 2.58 percent or our share of the council tax&nbsp;
bill if you like by 2.58 percent and I say it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.000
a difficult decision because it genuinely is for&nbsp;
all councillors and as an organisation as a whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.560
we've had to very carefully balance the fact that&nbsp;
clearly our residents are facing increases in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:07.200
cost of living and pressures at home and we want&nbsp;
to keep Council tax as low as we possibly can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:13.200
to be as helpful as possible to our residents&nbsp;
but also we as an organisation are facing some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.800
of those pressures ourselves particularly rising&nbsp;
energy costs inflation and the like and so we've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:24.000
got to balance those out and we want to make sure&nbsp;
that we continue to provide really first-class&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:32.080
excellent services for the district um so we took&nbsp;
the decision to to to increase by 2.58 as i say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:37.040
it's below inflation and we hope that residents&nbsp;
will understand our reasons for doing so and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:42.080
we can continue to deliver a balanced budget and&nbsp;
excellent services for the district as a result

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:50.880
We've also recently found out the news that Derby&nbsp;
and Derbyshire have been named as a pathfinder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.200
for the government's new county deal scheme now&nbsp;
the government you'll have all heard about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:00.240
government referring to the to leveling up as as&nbsp;
being part of its agenda now the government's also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:05.200
published recently a leveling up white paper which&nbsp;
sets out in much more detail what they really mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:10.800
about levelling up and how they want to improve&nbsp;
areas like ours which have have suffered for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:16.320
for many years with historic under investment&nbsp;
by successive government so this is a real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:21.200
opportunity for North East Derbyshire and we&nbsp;
want to work with Derbyshire County Council and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:26.240
derby city council and all of the other borough&nbsp;
and district councils within Derbyshire to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.400
make sure that we get the best out of that deal&nbsp;
it's there's still a lot of detail to go through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.480
there's lots of negotiations happening with the&nbsp;
government around what that really means for us&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:39.120
but we'll continue to keep residents updated&nbsp;
but we're really excited about it we think it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:44.640
represents a really good opportunity to level up&nbsp;
in northeast Derbyshire and the wider county so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.880
we'll keep you posted but please keep a lookout&nbsp;
because it's a really exciting time for local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:55.840
government and for devolution in our area our&nbsp;
cabinet has also just approved a parking strategy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:04.160
for the district area we're committed to investing&nbsp;
280 000 pounds per year for the next several years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:10.160
to trying to find solutions to parking issues&nbsp;
particularly where we have large areas of council&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:16.240
housing in the district we know that we've got so&nbsp;
many different areas where parking is a problem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.040
where we've got lots of grassed areas for&nbsp;
example where there's absolutely minimal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.920
parking and residents find it really frustrating&nbsp;
that they just can't get parking spaces near to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:29.360
where they live so we're really keen to try&nbsp;
and address some of those issues and that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.240
what our parking strategy is seeking to do&nbsp;
moving on again the District Council has also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.680
announced now that it's going to increase&nbsp;
the fines for fly tipping and littering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:45.360
to the maximum amount that we're able to do so&nbsp;
within the legislation now we've always wanted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:49.600
to take a really tough stance against fly tipping&nbsp;
and littering because we know how important it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:56.080
to communities and how much of a blight it is&nbsp;
on our beautiful rural countryside surroundings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:00.480
so we think that this is part of a wider package&nbsp;
of measures we're trying to introduce to really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:05.920
crack down on fly tipping it happens far too&nbsp;
often there's absolutely no excuse for fly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:11.440
tipping or littering in this district and we want&nbsp;
to send a really loud and clear message to anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:16.720
thinking about doing that that it's absolutely not&nbsp;
acceptable we have also crushed a car a few months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:21.760
ago that was involved in in flight tipping and&nbsp;
again we hope that that's sending the that really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:28.240
clear message that it's just not acceptable to fly&nbsp;
tip your your rubbish in North East Derbyshire and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:32.400
we'll continue reviewing measures wherever we can&nbsp;
to ensure that we're taking the toughest possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:36.560
stance against that and increasing those fines is&nbsp;
just part of that and I think it's a really good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.520
thing that we've done there now keeping with the&nbsp;
theme of keeping our district looking beautiful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.520
we're also supporting the Great&nbsp;
British Spring Clean initiative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:49.600
this year we do it every year and basically&nbsp;
the Great British Spring Clean encourages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:55.280
all residents from across the country to do their&nbsp;
bit to help do some litter picking in their local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:00.480
community and help tidy it up really we we&nbsp;
do it every year as I say and our refuse team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:06.320
are able to provide all the kit litter pickers&nbsp;
bags uh the hoops to hold the bags in hi-vis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:12.320
jackets all the works that you'll need to do it we&nbsp;
have a lot of fantastic volunteer litter picking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:17.360
groups already in the district but we're always&nbsp;
keen to encourage more people to get involved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.680
i'll certainly be doing it at some stage this&nbsp;
spring as well and i think it's a really important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:26.960
year to do it in particularly with the the&nbsp;
Platinum Jubilee so i think if you can if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.000
you can do it if you're interested let's all get&nbsp;
together and help clean for The Queen now moving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.120
